{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "latlon3d_transport_cwc_mms",
    "description": "Method-of-manufactured-solutions driver for the CONSISTENT-WITH-CONTINUITY (CWC) vertical tracer transport pair on latlon3d -- the continuity rule grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lev_noflux_bc and the flux-form upwind rule grids/latlon3d/rules/upwind1_flux_D_lev_noflux_bc, coupled through the observed mixing ratio q = mq / m. Its companion problems/latlon3d_transport_cwc_freestream pins that a CONSTANT tracer is preserved bitwise; this one pins that a NON-CONSTANT tracer still converges at the donor-cell rate, i.e. that consistency with continuity was bought with a modelling fix and not with a loss of accuracy. \n\nTHE SYSTEM. \n    d(m)/dt  = -D(M, wrt: lev)   + src_m \n    d(mq)/dt = -D(M*q, wrt: lev) + src_mq,   q = mq / m \nwith m the air mass per unit area, mq the tracer mass, and M the face air-mass flux. The tracer operator never sees a velocity or a mixing-ratio field supplied from outside: it sees the mass flux and the ratio of the two states it is integrating, which is the entire point. \n\nFORCED-STEADY (TRUNCATION) IDIOM, following the sibling latlon3d_advection_vertical_upwind_flux. The manufactured solution is m*(z) = 2 - z and q*(z) = 1 + z^2, hence a tracer mass mq*(z) = (2 - z)(1 + z^2); the states are initialised to the EXACT CELL MEANS of m* and mq* (a finite-volume state is a cell mean, and seeding point values would inject an O(dz^2) error of its own -- the cell means are available in closed form because both profiles are polynomials). src_m and src_mq are the EXACT cell-mean flux divergences, which for a finite-volume cell are just differences of the exact face fluxes over the thickness, (M q*|_{k+1} - M q*|_k)/dz[k] -- no quadrature needed. In exact arithmetic the manufactured state is then a steady state of the forced system, so the drift measured at t = 0.1 IS the operator's truncation error and the observed convergence rate is the truncation order: 1, for donor-cell upwinding. \n\nTHE MASS EQUATION IS FROZEN, AND EXACTLY SO -- WHICH IS ITSELF A PIN. Because the discrete continuity operator is EXACT on cell means (the finite-volume divergence of exact face fluxes is the exact cell-mean divergence, identically), src_m -- written as the same difference of the same two face fluxes over the same dz -- cancels it BITWISE, term for term, including at the two walls where the wall flux is absent from the operator and where M vanishes exactly from the forcing. d(m)/dt is therefore exactly zero and m holds its initial cell means to the last bit. So the m-error assertion at t = 0.1 has a 1e-12 tolerance rather than a discretization-sized one: any drift at all in m would mean the continuity rule and the forcing disagree about which faces, which thicknesses, or which wall closure -- exactly the disagreement that destroys free-stream preservation in the companion problem. The tracer, by contrast, drifts at O(dz), because the donor-cell face value is a first-order reconstruction of q at the face while the forcing uses the exact one. \n\nWHY M VANISHES AT BOTH WALLS. The no-flux closure substitutes the exact wall flux (zero) instead of a reconstructed one, so a nonzero wall mass flux would leave an O(1) truncation error in the boundary cell that never vanishes under refinement (dividing a lone uncancelled O(dz) flux error by dz[1]). M = 4 z (1 - z)(1 - 2z) a(i) b(j) vanishes LINEARLY at each wall, so the flux at the first interior face is itself O(dz), the boundary flux error is O(dz^2), and the boundary cell stays O(dz) like the interior: the scheme is uniformly first order. It is also the only physically admissible wind -- air does not flow through the ground or the model lid. \n\nNLON and NLAT are pinned at both rule import edges; NLEV is left LIVE for the convergence harness to bind per resolution (and so the build-time ic/reference expressions, which cannot read observeds, can fold z from literals plus NLEV). The horizontal extents therefore appear as the literals 8 and 5 inside the runtime expressions.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:latlon3d",
      "op:advection",
      "op:div",
      "form:flux",
      "scheme:upwind",
      "axes:lev",
      "bc:no-flux",
      "mms:forced-steady"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Jockel, P., von Kuhlmann, R., Lawrence, M. G., et al. (2001). On a fundamental problem in implementing flux-form advection schemes for tracer transport in 3-dimensional general circulation and chemistry transport models. Quarterly Journal of the Royal Meteorological Society, 127(573), 1035-1052.",
        "doi": "10.1002/qj.49712757318"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2002). Finite Volume Methods for Hyperbolic Problems. Cambridge University Press. Section 4.1 (donor-cell upwind)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. Journal of Fluids Engineering, 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "TransportCWCMMS": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/face_flux_divergence_lev_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 8,
            "NLAT": 5
          }
        },
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon3d/rules/upwind1_flux_D_lev_noflux_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NLON": 8,
            "NLAT": 5
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "m": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "AIR MASS per unit area (pressure thickness dp); cell means of m*(z) = 2 - z. Held exactly steady by src_m, which cancels the continuity operator bitwise; any drift in m is a bug in the continuity rule."
        },
        "mq": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "TRACER MASS; cell means of mq*(z) = (2 - z)(1 + z^2). The convergence norm is measured on THIS state: its drift from the manufactured steady state at t = 0.1 is the donor-cell truncation error."
        },
        "pe": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Level-edge coordinate; pe[1] = 0 (ground), pe[NLEV+1] = 1 (model top). Stretched (0.6 s + 0.4 s^2, s = (kn-1)/NLEV) so the vertical mesh is genuinely non-uniform and cells are thin at the ground. Aggregate index `kn`, distinct from an operator's `k` (observeds are inlined non-hygienically).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "kn"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "kn": {
                "from": "lev_nodes"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.6,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    0.4,
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "/",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "-",
                          "args": [
                            "kn",
                            1
                          ]
                        },
                        "NLEV"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "dz": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Layer thicknesses dz[k] = pe[k+1] - pe[k], from the grid's lev_thickness template (aggregate index `gk`). Both the continuity divergence and the tracer flux divergence divide by THIS array, which is one of the three things the free-stream bit-exactness argument depends on (same faces, same thicknesses, same wall omissions).",
          "expression": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "lev_thickness",
            "bindings": {
              "pe": "pe"
            }
          }
        },
        "M": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Face AIR-MASS FLUX, positive upward: M = 4 z (1 - z)(1 - 2z) a(i) b(j). Vanishes exactly at both walls (required by the no-flux closure, and physically -- no air through the ground or the lid) and reverses sign at z = 1/2, so both donor branches are exercised in every column. The strictly positive horizontal modulation a(i) b(j) catches a stencil that mis-indexed M as a column profile.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "iw",
              "jw",
              "kw"
            ],
            "args": [
              "pe"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "iw": {
                "from": "lon"
              },
              "jw": {
                "from": "lat"
              },
              "kw": {
                "from": "lev_nodes"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    4.0,
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "pe",
                        "kw"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "-",
                      "args": [
                        1,
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "pe",
                            "kw"
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "-",
                      "args": [
                        1,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            2,
                            {
                              "op": "index",
                              "args": [
                                "pe",
                                "kw"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    1,
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        0.25,
                        {
                          "op": "cos",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                6.283185307179586,
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "-",
                                      "args": [
                                        "iw",
                                        0.5
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    8
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    1,
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        0.2,
                        {
                          "op": "sin",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                3.141592653589793,
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    {
                                      "op": "-",
                                      "args": [
                                        "jw",
                                        1
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    4
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "q": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "The MIXING RATIO q = mq / m: tracer mass divided by air mass, cell by cell. It is a BARE declared observed of shape [lon, lat, lev], which is exactly what the advection rule's esm-spec 9.6.1 `where` constraint demands -- a shape constraint is satisfied only by a bare variable reference, never by a compound sub-AST, so the equation MUST be written D(M*q) over a declared q rather than D(M*mq/m) inline. This single indirection is the whole of consistency with continuity: the tracer flux is built from the ratio to a mass the model actually carries. Aggregate indices `iq,jq,kq`, distinct from the operator's `i,j,k`.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "iq",
              "jq",
              "kq"
            ],
            "args": [
              "mq",
              "m"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "iq": {
                "from": "lon"
              },
              "jq": {
                "from": "lat"
              },
              "kq": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "mq",
                    "iq",
                    "jq",
                    "kq"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "m",
                    "iq",
                    "jq",
                    "kq"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "src_m": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "MMS forcing for the AIR MASS: the exact cell-mean divergence of the face mass flux, (M[k+1] - M[k])/dz[k]. Written as the same difference of the same two face values over the same thickness that face_flux_divergence_lev_noflux_bc emits, so it cancels the operator BITWISE and holds m exactly steady -- at the walls too, because M vanishes there exactly and the operator's wall term is absent. Aggregate indices `ia,ja,ka`.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "ia",
              "ja",
              "ka"
            ],
            "args": [
              "M",
              "dz"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "ia": {
                "from": "lon"
              },
              "ja": {
                "from": "lat"
              },
              "ka": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "M",
                        "ia",
                        "ja",
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            "ka",
                            1
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "M",
                        "ia",
                        "ja",
                        "ka"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "dz",
                    "ka"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "src_mq": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "MMS forcing for the TRACER MASS: the EXACT cell-mean flux divergence (M q*|_{k+1} - M q*|_k)/dz[k] with the exact face mixing ratio q*(z) = 1 + z^2 read at the level edges. Unlike src_m this does NOT cancel the operator -- the operator's donor-cell face value is a first-order reconstruction of q, the forcing's is exact -- and the O(dz) residue is precisely the truncation error the convergence case measures. Aggregate indices `ib,jb,kb`.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "ib",
              "jb",
              "kb"
            ],
            "args": [
              "M",
              "pe",
              "dz"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "ib": {
                "from": "lon"
              },
              "jb": {
                "from": "lat"
              },
              "kb": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "M",
                            "ib",
                            "jb",
                            {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                "kb",
                                1
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            1,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "index",
                                  "args": [
                                    "pe",
                                    {
                                      "op": "+",
                                      "args": [
                                        "kb",
                                        1
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "index",
                                  "args": [
                                    "pe",
                                    {
                                      "op": "+",
                                      "args": [
                                        "kb",
                                        1
                                      ]
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "index",
                          "args": [
                            "M",
                            "ib",
                            "jb",
                            "kb"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            1,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "index",
                                  "args": [
                                    "pe",
                                    "kb"
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "index",
                                  "args": [
                                    "pe",
                                    "kb"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "dz",
                    "kb"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      },
